{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790264958,"nonce":"MO0VXnwg59aLNr4rNogTEje9Uz0=","title":"GPU plugin: browser runtime, mobile window handles and runtime checks off Apple","message":"The GPU plugin compiles for Metal, DX12, Vulkan, Android Vulkan/GLES, browser\nWebGPU and Emscripten GLES, and clippy passes for Windows MSVC and Linux\nx86_64. Only Apple M1 Pro/Metal has run the fixtures.\n\n- Run the gpu and window_gpu fixtures on Windows DX12, desktop Vulkan and\n  GLES; Android; and browser WebGPU. Feature-gated parts (binding arrays,\n  external textures, ray queries, mesh shaders) run where the adapter has them.\n- The browser needs Caribou's wasm runtime to register the plugin statically\n  and to hand over an HTML or offscreen canvas.\n- The window plugin gives desktop handles only; Android and iOS need\n  providers.\n- Threaded wasm needs a decision on the resource tables' thread model; today\n  the single-threaded build relies on wgpu's fragile Send/Sync.\n- Conformance fixtures for cancellation and early settlement of futures and\n  for resource destruction and leaks.\n\nSplit out of e61c43c, which covered the API surface.","files":null}]}